

DB_PASSWORD=change_me
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change_me

# In the official:

# DB_PASSWORD=taskpass
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin123

# Files related
# compose.yaml → reads DB_PASSWORD and ADMIN_PASSWORD from .env.
# task-manager-api/src/main/.../SecurityConfig.java → reads ADMIN_PASSWORD for the admin API user.
# compose.yaml → passes DB_PASSWORD to PostgreSQL and to Spring Boot.

# The values of .env need to match credentials the project expect
# ADMIN_PASSWORD comes from SecurityConfig.java: the username is hardcoded as admin
# So the ADMIN_PASSWORD needs to match the value in App.jsx (Line: const authHeader = 'Basic ' + btoa('admin:admin123'))

# DB_PASSWORD does not come from SecurityConfig.java; it is used by compose.yaml/Spring Boot to authenticate with PostgreSQL.
# So for DB_PASSWORD, we can define any value, that will be in compose.yaml